---
[`zml.Buffer`](https://github.com/zml/zml/blob/8fcff8c462070d06056f8a85ba0c8a81f0f3a636/zml/buffer.zig)
holds backend handles for a concrete tensor. Create the inputs on the platform
used to compile your executable. The `io` argument is a `std.Io`, and
`allocator` is a `std.mem.Allocator`. A return type with `!` can carry an error.

# [Follow a buffer transfer]($heading.id('transfer-example'))

Use the input tensor's `shape` and matching host `bytes` with the platform that will run the model.

```=html
<div class="buffer-walkthrough">
  <fieldset class="command-tabs buffer-steps">
    <legend>Transfer stage</legend>
    <label class="command-tab"><input type="radio" name="buffer-stage" id="buffer-step-upload" aria-controls="buffer-example buffer-rule-upload" checked><span>Start transfer</span></label>
    <label class="command-tab"><input type="radio" name="buffer-stage" id="buffer-step-ready" aria-controls="buffer-example buffer-rule-ready"><span>Wait for device</span></label>
    <label class="command-tab"><input type="radio" name="buffer-stage" id="buffer-step-read" aria-controls="buffer-example buffer-rule-read"><span>Allocate readback</span></label>
    <label class="command-tab"><input type="radio" name="buffer-stage" id="buffer-step-release" aria-controls="buffer-example buffer-rule-release"><span>Release resources</span></label>
  </fieldset>
  <div id="buffer-example" class="command-shell buffer-example">
    <span class="command-language icon-code">Zig</span>
    <pre><code data-copy-label="Copy the Buffer transfer example"><span data-buffer-line="upload"><span class="token keyword">var</span> buffer = <span class="token keyword">try</span> zml.Buffer.<span class="token function">fromBytesOpts</span>(
    io,
    platform,
    shape,
    bytes,
    .{ .wait = <span class="token boolean">false</span> },
);</span>
<span data-buffer-line="release"><span class="token keyword">defer</span> buffer.<span class="token function">deinit</span>();</span>

<span data-buffer-line="ready"><span class="token keyword">try</span> buffer.<span class="token function">await</span>(io);</span>

<span data-buffer-line="read"><span class="token keyword">const</span> host = <span class="token keyword">try</span> buffer.<span class="token function">toSliceAlloc</span>(allocator, io);</span>
<span data-buffer-line="release"><span class="token keyword">defer</span> host.<span class="token function">free</span>(allocator);</span>
</code></pre>
  </div>
  <div class="buffer-rules" aria-live="polite">
    <p id="buffer-rule-upload" data-buffer-stage="upload">With <code>.wait = false</code>, keep <code>bytes</code> alive and unchanged until <code>buffer.await(io)</code> succeeds.</p>
    <p id="buffer-rule-ready" data-buffer-stage="ready">After <code>await</code> succeeds, the device buffer is ready and you can reuse or release the source bytes.</p>
    <p id="buffer-rule-read" data-buffer-stage="read"><code>toSliceAlloc</code> returns a separate host slice that you own.</p>
    <p id="buffer-rule-release" data-buffer-stage="release"><code>host.free(allocator)</code> releases the readback using the same allocator. <code>buffer.deinit()</code> releases the device handle.</p>
  </div>
</div>
```

# [Create device buffers]($heading.id('buffer'))

- `zml.Buffer.fromSlice(io, platform, slice)`\
  `!Buffer`. Copy a `zml.Slice` from host memory and wait for transfer.
- `zml.Buffer.fromBytes(io, platform, shape, bytes)`\
  `!Buffer`. Copy host bytes using the supplied `Shape`. The bytes must match its element type and size.

# [Inspect the shape and wait for transfers]($heading.id('shape-and-readiness'))

- `buffer.shape()`\
  `Shape`. Read the buffer's metadata.
- `buffer.await(io)`\
  `!void`. Wait for the backend buffer to become ready.

When using `fromSliceOpts` or `fromBytesOpts` with `.wait = false`, keep the
source bytes alive and unchanged until `buffer.await(io)` completes successfully.

# [Read back to host memory]($heading.id('read-back-to-host-memory'))

- `buffer.getValue(T, io)`\
  `!T`. Read back into a host type with matching representation and byte size. It copies bytes without converting the element type.
- `buffer.toSliceAlloc(allocator, io)`\
  `!Slice`. Read back into an owned host slice. Release it with `slice.free(allocator)`.

# [Release the buffer]($heading.id('release-the-buffer'))

- `buffer.deinit()`\
  `void`. Release the buffer through a mutable handle.

See [Load and inspect model weights]($link.page('zml/developer-guide/load-and-inspect-model-weights')) for an example of loading weights into device buffers.
